    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Roof damage insurance claims in San Antonio usually start with weather. Bexar County has logged 618 hail reports and 309 thunderstorm wind reports in the NOAA Storm Events Database, and roofs absorb most of that punishment. A roof claim can look simple from the ground and turn complicated on the roof: the insurer's estimate may cover a few shingles while the property owner sees a roof that needs replacing.</p>
<p>This page walks through how roof claims work, the policy terms that shape what gets paid, and where a public adjuster in San Antonio may help. If hail is the cause, our <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">San Antonio hail damage claims</a> page goes deeper on storm dating and hail-specific disputes.</p>

<h2>Roof Types We See Around San Antonio</h2>
<p>Different roofs fail in different ways, and insurers look for different things on each.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Roof type</th><th>Common storm damage</th><th>Common dispute</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
